# The styleguide page renders components directly from its own Fluid
# template and ignores anything editors place on the page - per the contract
# it has "no content areas". That cannot mean an empty "config.backend_layout"
# though:
#
# - "PageTsBackendLayoutDataProvider::generateBackendLayoutFromTsConfig()"
#   only registers a layout at all if "config.backend_layout." parses to a
#   non-empty array; a genuinely empty block would drop the layout from the
#   selector entirely, which is worse than a layout with an unused column.
# - A "rows" key present but empty produces a "Grid" with zero "GridRow"s.
#   "Partials/PageLayout/Grid.fluid.html" then renders a "<table>" with no
#   rows at all - no "new content element" affordance anywhere, i.e. the page
#   module becomes unusable for this layout, which is exactly the outcome the
#   task asked to avoid.
#
# So this ships one column that is deliberately not part of the colPos
# contract (0, 1, 2, 10-14 are all spoken for by the other layouts): colPos
# 999 is not read by any "lib.content.*" TypoScript object, so anything an
# editor drops here is stored but never rendered - inert, not broken. The
# label says so explicitly rather than reusing "main", which would suggest
# it behaves like the other layouts' main column.
mod.web_layout.BackendLayouts.styleguide {
    title = LLL:EXT:theme_extension_development/Resources/Private/Language/locallang.xlf:backendLayout.styleguide.title
    config.backend_layout {
        colCount = 1
        rowCount = 1
        rows.1.columns.1 {
            name = LLL:EXT:theme_extension_development/Resources/Private/Language/locallang.xlf:backendLayout.colPos.unused.name
            identifier = unused
            colPos = 999
        }
    }
}
